{"term":"possess","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9ebbd4267cd6af0bfc","definition":"To have (something) as, or as if as, an owner; to have, to own.","example":"He does not even possess a working telephone.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["inhold"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:547324b2c6f177ef24","definition":"Of an idea, thought, etc.: to dominate (someone's mind); to strongly influence.","example":"I am poſſeſt with an adulterate blot, / My bloud is mingled with the crime of luſt: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b244084409770b19a9","definition":"Of a supernatural entity, especially one regarded as evil: to take control of (an animal or person's body or mind).","example":"They thought he was possessed by evil spirits.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6703ad63f151b2e471","definition":"Of a person: to control or dominate (oneself or someone, or one's own or someone's heart, mind, etc.).","example":"Resolving to possess myself in some quiet if it might be, in a time of so great jealosy, I built by my Brother's permission a study, made a fishpond, an island, and some other solitudes and retirements, at Wotton, which gave the first occasion of improving them to those water-works and gardens which afterwards succeeded them.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, literary, poetic, reflexive","register":"also, literary, poetic, reflexive, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cf3947b69423540c1e","definition":"To cause an idea, thought, etc., to strongly affect or influence (someone); to inspire, to preoccupy.","example":"What on earth possessed you to go walking by the quarry at midnight?","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e9c4fb4cf8c4688f42","definition":"To occupy the attention or time of (someone).","example":"[W]hen he [Henry Wotton] was beyond ſeventy years of age he made this deſcription of a part of the preſent pleaſure that poſſeſt him, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9450100a22a8250a8d","definition":"To obtain or seize (something); to gain, to win.","example":"[T]hey in ſecret counſell cloſe conſpird, / How to effect ſo hard an enterprize, / And to poſſeſſe the purpoſe they deſird: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, archaic, literary","register":"also, archaic, literary, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f2d09e0e1acaba871","definition":"Chiefly followed by of or with: to vest ownership of something in (oneself or someone); to bestow upon, to endow.","example":"Lvcius Tarquinius (for his exceſſive pride ſurnamed Superbus) after hee had cauſed his owne father in law Seruius Tullius to be cruelly murdred, and contrarie to the Romaine lawes and cuſtomes, not requiring or ſtaying for the peoples ſuffrages, had poſſeſſed himſelfe of the kingdome: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["seise"],"antonyms":["dispossess","unpossess"],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, archaic, reflexive","register":"also, archaic, reflexive, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:534996d0db445b0371","definition":"To have control or possession of, but not to own (a chattel or an interest in land).","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:36e1d9e3402c63cd35","definition":"To give (someone) information or knowledge; to acquaint, to inform.","example":"I cannot bid you bid my daughter liue, / That were impoſſible, but I pray you both, / Poſſeſs the people in Meſſina here, / How innocent ſhe died, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4cf3964b2536d1b5bd","definition":"To have the ability to use, or knowledge of (a language, a skill, etc.)","example":"And Mr. Holt found that Harry could read and write, and poſſeſſed the two languages of French and Engliſh very well, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c5113dff9d730a7488","definition":"To inhabit or occupy (a place).","example":"[W]ell thou knowſt / God hath pronounc't it death to taſte that Tree, / The only ſign of our obedience left / Among ſo many ſignes of power and rule / Conferrd upon us, and Dominion giv'n / Over all other Creatures that poſſeſſe Earth, Aire, and Sea.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["have","hold","own","possess"],"antonyms":["go without","lose"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["adversely possess","mispossess","possessable","possessible","possessed","possessee","possessing","possessingly","prepossessing","repossess","unpossess","unpossessed","unpossessing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d40b36e105400363e1","definition":"Chiefly followed by that: to convince or persuade (someone).","example":"By ſuch malicious Inſinuations, he had poſſeſs'd the Lady, that he was the only Man in t